---
// SystemSection.astro — Hardware Diagnostics & Low-RAM Architecture
---
<section id="system" class="section-wrapper system-section" data-section="system">
  <div class="container-editorial">
    <div class="system-header">
      <span class="badge-tag">
        <span class="dot"></span>
        <span>05 // TELEMETRY HUD</span>
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-title anim-title">HARDWARE INTERROGATION WITHOUT MEMORY OVERHEAD.</h2>
      <p class="system-sub text-secondary anim-fade">
        The embedded System Info Card provides instantaneous awareness of hardware utilization. Built with Tauri 2 in Rust, the app maintains an ultralow footprint so your GPU and CPU cycles belong to your games.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="telemetry-dashboard anim-fade">
      <div class="hud-quadrant">
        <div class="quad-header text-mono">
          <span class="accent-signal">MONITOR 01</span>
          <span>CPU SCHEDULER</span>
        </div>
        <div class="quad-stat text-mono">LOCAL WMI INTERROGATION</div>
        <p class="quad-note text-secondary">
          Enumerates processor topology, thread allocation, and base frequency via native Windows APIs without background polling spikes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-quadrant">
        <div class="quad-header text-mono">
          <span class="accent-signal">MONITOR 02</span>
          <span>RAM CONSUMPTION</span>
        </div>
        <div class="quad-stat text-mono">&lt; 45 MB RESIDENT RAM</div>
        <p class="quad-note text-secondary">
          Tauri 2 replaces bloated Electron Chromium runtimes with the lightweight OS native WebView2 control, cutting idle memory by up to 85%.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-quadrant">
        <div class="quad-header text-mono">
          <span class="accent-signal">MONITOR 03</span>
          <span>GPU ADAPTER ENUM</span>
        </div>
        <div class="quad-stat text-mono">DIRECT HARDWARE ID</div>
        <p class="quad-note text-secondary">
          Identifies discrete and integrated graphics adapters to ensure your active graphics pipeline matches game minimum requirements.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-quadrant">
        <div class="quad-header text-mono">
          <span class="accent-signal">MONITOR 04</span>
          <span>OS KERNEL & TOAST</span>
        </div>
        <div class="quad-stat text-mono">PORTAL STACKING CONTEXT</div>
        <p class="quad-note text-secondary">
          System toast notifications render via top-level portals into the document body, guaranteeing zero occlusion by modals or overlays.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.system-section {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
}

.system-header {
  max-width: 860px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 4rem;
}

.system-sub {
  font-size: var(--font-16);
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.telemetry-dashboard {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: 2rem;
}

@media (max-width: 860px) {
  .telemetry-dashboard {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

.hud-quadrant {
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  background: rgba(12, 12, 14, 0.7);
  backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  padding: 2.2rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1rem;
}

.quad-header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
}

.quad-stat {
  font-size: 18px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

.quad-note {
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.6;
}
</style>
